# cytokine — inflammation (the response amplifies itself)
#
# the new mechanism, the one the first two models don't have: POSITIVE FEEDBACK.
# cytokines recruit immune cells, which release more cytokines. that is the cafe's
# self-reference — a flow INTO inflammation whose rate reads inflammation — and it
# turns a graded response into a switch with a threshold and HYSTERESIS.
#
# two inflows feed inflammation:
#   insult -> inflammation : reads pathogens   — the trigger (dial it)
#   tissue -> inflammation : reads inflammation — the self-amplification (cafe)
# and one outflow resolves it (anti-inflammatory clearance).
#
# because the response amplifies itself, the trigger to switch ON is HIGHER than
# the trigger to switch OFF, so the two branches differ (verified):
#   pathogen < ~12   -> resolves either way        (acute: returns to baseline)
#   pathogen > ~42   -> full inflammation either way
#   ~12 < pathogen < ~42 -> depends on HISTORY: a calm body stays calm, but an
#                            already-inflamed body STAYS inflamed
# that gap is why inflammation overshoots and can become CHRONIC: it ignites at
# ~42 but won't quit until the trigger falls below ~12, long after it lit.
#
# default below is a naive body hit with a big insult (pathogens 50) -> it ignites.
# drop pathogens into 12..42 and inflammation now depends on where you started:
# init inflammation at 0 (calm) vs 50 (primed) gives the two branches.
node inflammation : range(0, 50), init(0)   @ bucket(fill = dots)
node pathogens    : range(0, 100), init(50)            # the trigger — held, only read
external tissue                                         # resident cells (the amplifier)
external insult                                         # pathogen-driven kick
external resolve                                        # anti-inflammatory clearance

insult       -> inflammation : proportional(of = pathogens, k = 0.05)           # trigger
tissue       -> inflammation : hill(of = inflammation, max = 8, k = 25, n = 4)  # self-amplification
inflammation -> resolve      : proportional(of = inflammation, k = 0.2)         # resolution

pathway inflame : insult->inflammation, tissue->inflammation, inflammation->resolve
